WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.185 --> 00:00:01.810
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Today, we're talking

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:05.830
about zero trust, VPC service
controls, and a podcast

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:07.450
about the blog.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:08.440
I am Priyanka.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.540
And welcome to "This
Week in Cloud,"

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:14.140
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:16.960
We believe zero trust
is an effective way

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.440
to enhance overall security
and provide a better user

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:21.400
experience.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.250
And BeyondCorp Enterprise
can help make this possible.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.480
That's why we are excited to
announce three new BeyondCorp

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.020
Enterprise features designed
to help our customers provide

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.730
their users simple and secure
access to key applications--

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:40.240
certificate-based access
via VPC Service Controls,

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.110
on-prem connector, and easy
to configure custom access

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.080
policies.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.740
Google Cloud strives to be
the most trusted cloud, which

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:52.890
is why we are continuously
updating our protection

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.120
capabilities.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.960
In addition to IAP, we now
support VPC Service Controls

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:01.560
for Cloud Run, which creates
enterprise-grade security

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:05.040
guardrails protecting your
data at the network level

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:09.150
while delivering the ease
of use and speed to market.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.820
The Google Cloud tech
blog is a great resource

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:14.010
for all things happening
in Google Cloud.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:17.430
And if you prefer to listen
rather than read, check out

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:21.270
the "Google Cloud Reader"
podcast, available wherever

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.610
you listen to
podcasts, and enjoy

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:27.480
an audio version of the latest
and greatest with Google Cloud.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.000
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.770
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:36.160
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:38.810
We'll see you in the Cloud.

